# R2 (OPTIONAL, SOFT). IMAGE: tp4-speed-1 (exists; tp4/speed 9cac8a84: draft K/V slide on, no tile split, no tp4/draft). D1's sequence
# on c2-packed-tp4-gate: the checkout's and the image's gate profile agree (slide on in both), so the ramp check is valid.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over the job file on a throwaway
# commit of tp4/stack-fix (or a descendant) and push the window tag. Nothing here names a rig, a card or a registry. The smoke and its
# check run from the CHECKOUT on the rig host; the server is the IMAGE'S baked tree (--read-only, no bind mount), so C2_IMAGE_TAG picks
# the server and the checkout picks the smoke and the check. THE DRIVER SUBSTITUTES C2_IMAGE_TAG FROM ITS IMAGE_TAG ENV: a chain that
# sets one IMAGE_TAG for all its jobs runs every job on that image, so jobs that need different images are SEPARATE ONE-JOB CHAINS.
# READS: garbage in concurrent4_steady = the tile split (tp4/exact) is not needed for the defect; coherent = the tile split is part of
# the layout that breaks (it frees extra buffers inside the traced forward). A hang here is X3's signature (MMIO per-op timeout in
# _prefill_chunked_eager_tp): the cards need the next chain job's reset. The first-prefill ledger line (see G3) is expected on this
# image, so the run ends red whatever the text: a ONE-JOB chain, read by hand. Duration (estimate): 10-13 min, or the smoke step's
# timeout on a hang.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-speed-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady
